==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|k|i}}

===Etymology===
From Proto-Uralic *kira and verbal suffix [[-ta]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|ki|ro|ta|lang=fi}}
* Rhymes: [[virota]]
* {{IPA|lang=fi|/ˈkirotɑ(ʔ)/}}

===Verb===
{{fi-verb}}

# {{context|intransitive|lang=fi}} To [[curse]], [[swear]], [[damn]].
# {{context|transitive|+ genitive-accusative|lang=fi}} To [[curse]] sb, [[cast]] a [[spell]] over sb/sth, [[enchant]] sb (''negatively'').

====Conjugation====
{{fi-conj-katketa|kir|||o}}

====Usage notes====
* The frequentative verb {{term|kiroilla|lang=fi}} is used when the cursing lasts longer, is continuous, is temporally more or less indefinite or the cursing is a habit. On the other hand, {{term||kirota|lang=fi}} is used, for example, when a person says one or a few naughty words in a particular situation. The difference can sometimes be translated in English by using the continuous aspect.

====Related terms====
* nouns: [[kirous]]
* verbs: ''frequentative'' [[kiroilla]]

